WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.416 --> 00:00:03.931
- [Narrator] Meet Mawson and Tingoora,

00:00:03.931 --> 00:00:05.681
two adorable dingoes.

00:00:07.633 --> 00:00:09.516
No, these aren't pet dogs.

00:00:09.516 --> 00:00:12.253
They're actually wild animals.

00:00:12.253 --> 00:00:14.761
Dingoes are Australia's wild dog,

00:00:14.761 --> 00:00:17.575
considered a cultural icon

00:00:17.575 --> 00:00:19.212
but due to interbreeding,

00:00:19.212 --> 00:00:22.534
pure dingoes have become harder to spot.

00:00:22.534 --> 00:00:25.682
Hence both Morrison and
Tingora's similar appearance

00:00:25.682 --> 00:00:27.099
to domestic dogs.

00:00:28.278 --> 00:00:31.010
Dingoes are thought to have
been introduced to Australia

00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:34.143
three to four thousand years ago.

00:00:34.143 --> 00:00:37.725
They are Australia's largest
terrestrial predator.

00:00:37.725 --> 00:00:39.946
Dingoes hunt everything.

00:00:39.946 --> 00:00:44.214
From rodents and birds to
larger prey, like kangaroos.

00:00:44.214 --> 00:00:47.949
They are a big part of
aboriginal Australian culture

00:00:47.949 --> 00:00:51.395
yet are seen as pests by livestock farmers

00:00:51.395 --> 00:00:54.768
due to perceived attacks on animals.

00:00:54.768 --> 00:00:57.001
Hunting for their skin and interbreeding

00:00:57.001 --> 00:01:00.284
has left their population vulnerable.

00:01:00.284 --> 00:01:01.784
This is the dingo.

